data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"filePath\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/d002-reply.md\", \"content\": \"# d002 reply\\n\\nImplemented the dispatch exactly as asked, in `~/subject` on branch\\n`cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>` (commit `deb4861` \\\"Add greet function\\nand unittest tests\\\").\\n\\n## What I did\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` — defines `greet(name)` returning `f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`, so\\n   `greet(\\\"Ada\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"`.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` — a `unittest.TestCase` with two tests:\\n   - `test_normal_name`: `greet(\\\"Ada\\\") == \\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"`\\n   - `test_empty_string`: `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`\\n   The test file prepends `../src` to `sys.path` so `unittest discover` works\\n   from the repo root.\\n3. Ran the tests myself.\\n\\n## Test command and result\\n\\nCommand (run from `~/subject`):\\n\\n    python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n\\nOutput and exit status:\\n\\n    ..\\n    ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    Ran 2 tests in 0.001s\\n\\n    OK\\n    exit=0\\n\\nExit status: **0** (no failures, no errors).\\n\\n## Commit\\n\\nWork is committed on my own branch:\\n\\n    deb4861 Add greet function and unittest tests\\n    2eda3b0 base\\n\\nWorking tree clean (only removed transient `__pycache__` dirs after the run).\\n\\nNothing blocked; nothing left undone.\\n\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_10","index":1,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1789938742,"id":"chatcmpl-baf9419a3330454a84b9e9389ed38b76","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

